      "message": "[error] Line 684: 🔴 The new DTLS tests hard-depend on certificate/key files under `tools/asterisk/keys` via `__FILE__`-derived paths, but they never check that those fixtures exist before using them. When the files are missing in a given CI/layout, `fileutils::loadFile(...)`/account config fails as an exception/error path, which can abort the test run instead of producing a controlled test outcome. Add explicit `std::filesystem::exists` checks for all required fixtures and fail/skip with a clear message (or move these fixtures into test-managed assets copied by the build). This improves cross-platform reliability and likely addresses the observed multi-platform CI failures.",
